## Context

Follow-up from the merged-ref /roar sweep of PR1713 and PR1714 at
3b19801c1946670ddcd4952cba21133699cab970. Parent1654 remains open.
The public live intake contract now documents selected-policy and assessed
poor-input restrictions. The selection module docstring still states at
scripts/_rel_reasons.py:38 that synthesis is for works “with an abstract”.
That blanket statement contradicts its correct implementation at lines315–322:
an included nonempty selected-policy record is bibliometric_only, as is an
included assessed absent/nonabstract/truncated input. This is documentation
of an actual method, rather than a proposal for another guard.

## Scope

Correct only the module's evidence-use explanation. Preserve the dated raw
trimmed-empty rule, membership/exclusion semantics and historical provenance.
Do not alter implementation, policy scope, model outputs or corpus data.

## Exit criteria

- The module docstring agrees with docs/rel-intake-contract.md: selected policy
  and assessed absent/nonabstract/truncated inputs restrict included works to
  bibliometric_only even with nonempty text; independently excluded rel_use
  remains blank.
- Explain that restrictions follow actually selected assessments and that an
  ICF update alone cannot clear a still-selected dimension policy.
- Preserve the raw-empty abstract flag and mu/rel_reason/rel_final semantics.
  Verify executable AST unchanged and run the sufficient documentation gate.

